+\subsection{Prospective validation studies}
+\label{sec:prospective}
+Two further studies were specified, with their samples, levels, tolerances, endpoints and
+analyses, before any of their outcomes were tracked (Supplement S1.16). The first re-tracks
+historical primary evaluations. The 4,800 primary evaluations were stratified by method, matched
+group, production-profile feasibility, search stage (evaluations 1--80 or 81--160) and distance
+to the nearest diagnostic limit (threshold-normalized margin at most or above 0.1). Simple random
+sampling without replacement selected two evaluations from each nonempty stratum, or all of a
+smaller one, giving 387 settings: 132 constraint-aware, 129 unconstrained and 126 scalarized.
+Each was tracked at the production resolution and at four refined levels. The fixed-source
+medium and fine levels keep the production source file and use 48- or 64-cell grids with half
+or a quarter of both integration steps; the combined medium and fine levels additionally use
+\num{20000} or \num{40000} particles from the reconstructed source. Production-level reruns had
+to reproduce the archived values before refinement. Per-run feasible fractions are weighted by
+the inclusion probabilities and have stratified design variances. Paired differences use
+ten-group bootstrap intervals conditional on the sampled observations, reported with the design
+standard errors. The declared tolerances between the medium and fine levels are \SI{1}{\percent}
+of each size, divergence and bunch-length limit, \SI{0.01}{\mega\electronvolt} in mean energy,
+$10^{-4}$ in transmission and a \SI{1}{\percent} relative change in each objective; they are
+adequacy thresholds, not error bounds.
+
+The second study runs ten matched pairs of new constraint-aware campaigns (groups 42--51) of
+160 evaluations each, with the production configuration, source and resolution, identical
+initial Sobol designs, model fitting and acquisition budgets, and per-iteration random streams
+shared within each pair. One arm uses the raw residuals of Sec.~\ref{sec:acquisition}; the other
+divides each residual by its threshold scale ($10^{-3}$ for sizes, divergences and bunch length,
+\SI{5}{\mega\electronvolt} for each energy side and 0.1 for transmission), at the same
+dimensionless temperature $10^{-3}$. Its physical smoothing widths are therefore
+\SI{1}{\micro\metre}, \SI{1}{\micro\radian}, \SI{5}{\kilo\electronvolt} and $10^{-4}$ in
+transmission, against \SI{1}{\milli\metre}, \SI{1}{\milli\radian}, \SI{0.001}{\electronvolt} and
+$10^{-3}$ for the raw arm, so the comparison changes the relative widths as well as the units.
+The campaigns ran one at a time, alternating which arm of a pair ran first. The predeclared
+endpoint is the paired normalized-minus-raw feasible fraction over all 160 evaluations; the
+fraction after initialization is a supporting endpoint. Both use ten-group percentile bootstrap
+intervals. Neither study used pilot tuning or outcome-dependent stopping or expansion.
+
