+\SI{0.9}{\percent}. No unconstrained or scalarized classification changed, and no feasible
+evaluation became infeasible. The weighted constraint-aware feasible fraction therefore rises
+from 0.405 to 0.460 (design standard error 0.027) at the fine levels, while the baseline
+fractions are unchanged. The paired differences over all 160 evaluations, 0.303 against
+unconstrained MOBO and 0.335 against scalarized BO at both fine levels, are positive in all ten
+groups, compared with 0.248 and 0.280 at the production resolution.
